# sirius: launchd stops at the missing dyld shared cache (2026-10-28 13:50 capture)
#
# Kernel: 8091fb20f0613d82a34df6467f05a4df6d8107dbd758e2a48753ff867f42c41d, i.e. the build
# before sirius-systemos-union.patch. Captured from /dev/ttyACM0 (the CDC-ACM ring; a host byte
# replays the whole ring, so the raw 3.4 MB capture holds the boot twice — this is the trimmed
# form; raw file was .scratch/console-now.log).
#
# What it shows: the OS volume mounts (disk2s1), AMFI latches its PMGR and lets launchd exec,
# launchd issues 24 syscalls, and then every dyld cache path is ENOENT while /usr/lib/dyld and
# /sbin/launchd resolve. The cache lives in the SystemOS cryptex volume, which this boot does not
# mount — that is the stop this port is now fixing.
